2. Cisco IOS CLI Mode Hierarchy (Core Exam Concept)

The video emphasizes that typing a command in the wrong mode will result in an
error:

User EXEC Mode          --> Router>            (Read-only, basic ping/tests)
   ↓ (enable)
Privileged EXEC Mode    --> Router#            (Full view, diagnostics, show commands)
   ↓ (configure terminal)
Global Config Mode      --> Router(config)#    (Device-wide changes, hostnames, routing)
   ↓ (interface <name>)
Interface Config Mode   --> Router(config-if)# (Specific port IP, clock rate, no shutdown)

  - Use exit to step back one level.
  - Use end or Ctrl + Z to jump straight back to Privileged EXEC (Router#).

3. Router Memory Architecture (High Viva Probability)

| Memory Type | Survives Reboot?       | What is Stored Here                                                                          |
| :---------- | :--------------------: | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **ROM**     | **Yes**                | Bootstrap program (boots the router before the OS loads), basic diagnostic software (POST).  |
| **FLASH**   | **Yes**                | Cisco IOS software image (permanent OS storage).                                             |
| **RAM**     | **No** (Volatile)      | Active workspace: `running-config`, routing tables, ARP cache, buffers. Wiped on power loss. |
| **NVRAM**   | **Yes** (Non-volatile) | `startup-config` (the saved configuration loaded at boot).                                   |

Key Rule from Video: Any change you make lives only in RAM (running-config). If
power cuts or the router reboots, all work is lost unless copied into NVRAM
(startup-config).

4. Comprehensive Command List: Question-by-Question (a) to (l)

| Part    | Objective                                   | Cisco IOS Command                                                           | Mode Required     | What it Does / What Output to Look For                                                                                                                        |
| :-----: | :------------------------------------------ | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :---------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **(a)** | **Know mode & switch to Privileged**        | `enable`                                                                    | `Router>`         | Prompt flips from `Router>` to `Router#`.                                                                                                                     |
| **(b)** | **Switch to Configuration mode**            | `configure terminal`<br>*(or `conf t`)*                                     | `Router#`         | Prompt flips to `Router(config)#`.                                                                                                                            |
| **(c)** | **Obtain router info (OS, RAM, stats)**     | `show version`                                                              | `Router#`         | Displays IOS Version (e.g., `15.1`), uptime, main RAM size, NVRAM size, interfaces count, and Configuration Register (`0x2102`).                              |
| **(d)** | **Status of routing protocols**             | `show ip protocols`                                                         | `Router#`         | Shows active routing engine (e.g., `Routing Protocol is "rip"`), update timers (30 sec), networks advertised, and administrative distance (`120`).            |
| **(e)** | **Show routing table**                      | `show ip route`                                                             | `Router#`         | Shows route codes: `C` (Directly Connected), `L` (Local interface IP), `R` (Learned via RIP), `S` (Static).                                                   |
| **(f)** | **Save running configuration**              | `copy running-config startup-config`<br>*(or `write`)*                      | `Router#`         | Commits changes from RAM to NVRAM. Prompts `Destination filename [startup-config]?` $\rightarrow$ press **Enter**.                                            |
| **(g)** | **View command history**                    | `show history`                                                              | `Router#`         | Shows the last 10 commands typed. (Use the **Up/Down arrow keys** as a shortcut).                                                                             |
| **(h)** | **View & set router clock**                 | `show clock`<br>`clock set hh:mm:ss DD Month YYYY`                          | `Router#`         | Routers have no battery clock. Run `clock set 10:00:00 26 Sep 2026` so system event logs have accurate timestamps.                                            |
| **(i)** | **View list of hosts**                      | `show hosts`                                                                | `Router#`         | Shows static name-to-IP mappings entered manually via `ip host <name> <ip>`.                                                                                  |
| **(j)** | **Interface statistics (Detailed & Brief)** | **Detailed:** `show interfaces`<br><br>**Brief:** `show ip interface brief` | `Router#`         | • **Detailed:** Full MTU, bandwidth, duplex, encapsulation (HDLC vs ARPA), error packets.<br>• **Brief:** One-line summary: IP address, Status, and Protocol. |
| **(k)** | **Know controller type (DTE or DCE)**       | `show controllers Serial0/3/0`                                              | `Router#`         | Look for the specific line: `DCE V.35, clock rate 64000` or `DTE V.35`.                                                                                       |
| **(l)** | **Configure Ethernet & Serial interfaces**  | *(See code block below)*                                                    | `Router(config)#` | Sets IP, subnet mask, DCE clock rate, and administratively enables ports with `no shutdown`.                                                                  |

